subproblems.statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ, let w = (w_1, …, w_m) (w : Fin m → Euclid P) be an orthonormal family in ℝ^P, let a ∈ ℝ^P, and let S := {y ∈ ℝ^P : y − a ∈ span{w_1, …, w_m}}. Let J : (Fin m → ℝ) → ℝ^P, J(z) := a + Σ_i z_i·w_i, where Fin m → ℝ carries its product Lebesgue measure volume, and let H^m := μHE[m]. Then:
(i) the push-forward of volume under J is H^m restricted to S: (volume).map J = H^m⌞S;
(ii) S is closed;
(iii) (H^m⌞S)(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ ℝ^P;
(iv) (H^m⌞S)(B_r(a)) > 0 for every r > 0, where B_r(a) is the open ball of radius r about a.
